    "parts": [],
    "answer_text": "Stems of various plants have undergone modifications to perform different functions. Underground stems or storage stems include rhizomes, corms, and tubers. For example, in ginger and banana, the underground stem is called a rhizome. The underground stem in Colocasia (arvi) is known as corm. Rhizomes and corms are underground stems, modified for the storage of food. The potato is a tuber that helps in the storage of food and bears eyes on it. Supportive stems, like tendrils, help the plant get attached to nearby structures for support. The stem in bougainvillea and citrus plants bear sharp, pointed structures called thorns for protection.",
    "answer_latex": null,
    "steps": [],
    "final_answer": "Thus, stems can modify for storage, support, and protection.",
