      "source_image_index": null,
      "ownership": "unknown"
    },
    "parts": [],
    "answer_text": "Inflorescence is the manner in which the flowers are arranged on the flowering axis. During the flowering season, the vegetative apex of the stem gets converted into a floral meristem. Based on whether the floral axis continues to grow or end in a flower, inflorescence is classified into racemose and cymose. In racemose inflorescence, the floral axis continues to grow and produces flowers laterally. On the other hand, in cymose inflorescence, the main axis terminates into a flower. Hence, it is limited in growth.",
    "answer_latex": null,
    "steps": [],
    "final_answer": "Thus, inflorescence can be classified into racemose and cymose based on the growth pattern of the floral axis.",
    "answer_image": {
